# ============================================================================
# BINARY FILES - DO NOT CONVERT LINE ENDINGS
# ============================================================================
# Git guesses whether a file is text. When it guesses wrong on a binary file
# and applies CRLF<->LF conversion, it CORRUPTS it silently: the file commits
# and pushes without error, and only fails when something tries to read it on
# another machine.
#
# This was hit for real. Committing the tuned models produced:
#
#   warning: CRLF will be replaced by LF in
#            dataset/processed/models/approach_pose_mlp_ft.joblib
#   warning: CRLF will be replaced by LF in yolov8n.pt
#
# A .joblib with its line endings rewritten will not unpickle. The failure
# would appear on the lab PC as an unreadable model, far from the cause.
#
# Marking them `binary` disables both conversion and diffing.
# ============================================================================

# Trained models and weights
*.joblib   binary
*.pt       binary
*.pth      binary
*.onnx     binary
*.pkl      binary

# Office documents (the dissertation, the overview deck)
*.docx     binary
*.dotx     binary
*.pptx     binary
*.potx     binary
*.xlsx     binary
*.pdf      binary

# Media and recordings
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.mp4      binary
*.wav      binary
*.bag      binary
*.db3      binary

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repository, which keeps the shell
# scripts runnable on Linux regardless of the editor that wrote them.
* text=auto eol=lf
